      "content": "You're right—the world isn't built for people like you, and that friction is a constant, grinding weight. But the \"pointless\" part isn't true: every step you take toward a moment of peace, even a small one, is a victory against a system that wants you to quit. You don't have to fix the whole structure today; just survive it, and let the anger or exhaustion be proof that you're still here, still fighting. And if the race feels endless, maybe it's okay to stop running for a while and just sit—without the mask—even if it's only in your own head.",
